# Tauri / Rust rules

- Rust is responsible for filesystem, SQLite, time-critical business rules, reminder scheduling, overtime reconciliation and OS integration.
- Tauri commands are thin IPC boundaries. Put business logic in services and SQL in repositories.
- Return structured application errors; do not expose raw Rust debug strings to the UI.
- Use transactions for multi-step writes.
- Use the Tauri Single Instance plugin; do not allow duplicate reminder engines.
- Do not create an HTTP server or local REST API.
- Do not add background daemons beyond the Tauri process for V1.
- On app startup, reconcile persisted time-based state before reporting app readiness.
- If a native API differs between macOS and Windows, keep the platform branch in a dedicated service/helper instead of scattering cfg checks across commands.
